module v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt

import v2.std.algebra { Empty, list_flat_map, any }
import v2.std.collection { List }
import v2.std.text { String }

// THE OVER-COST WITHHOLDING MECHANISM, CURRENTLY CARRYING NO IDENTITIES.
//
// WHY IT IS NOT THE EXPECTED-RED ROSTER, stated first because the two are easy to fuse.
//
// Any identity enrolled here is a witness that PASSES and whose MARGINAL cost exceeds
// `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_floor_claim_cpu_safety_limit_ms`. That is a different
// fact from a known red, and it may not ride the same carrier:
// `v2.workflow.floor_expected_red`'s own header states the bar it enforces -- "ENROLLING AN
// IDENTITY ASSERTS THAT IT REACHES ITS SUBJECT AND ANSWERS" -- and a withheld row answers
// nothing. Enrolling a green over-cost row there would assert a red that does not exist.
//
// THE MEASUREMENT BASIS IS MARGINAL COST, AND THAT SENTENCE IS THE WHOLE OF WHY THIS ROSTER WAS
// REBUILT ONCE BEFORE IT LANDED. The first cut of this population was discovered from main run
// 33109071348 at aea5e0dfd (15:34). `v1_compiler.cli_run` `run_claim_measured` began SUBTRACTING
// shared-artifact fill from a claim's charged CPU at gunbc#9477, which landed at 18:49 -- three
// hours after that measurement. So the first roster was built from CHARGED figures, in which a
// claim that happened to touch a shared artifact first was billed the entire fill.
//
// THE ERROR WAS NOT SMALL AND IT WAS NOT UNIFORM: of the 320 identities that population held,
// 119 -- 37% -- measure at or under the ceiling once fill is attributed to the artifact instead.
// The extremes are the tell. `test.claim.alias_identity_across_unwrap_witness`
// `a_second_alias_still_emits_its_own_name_and_not_the_first` was the SECOND most expensive row
// in the corpus at 4250ms charged; its marginal cost is 0ms. It never cost anything. Freezing it
// would have deleted a working witness's coverage, at identity grain, under a shrink-only
// contract that makes a wrong entry expensive to walk back -- and it would have looked exactly
// like a correct entry from the inside, because the number was real.
//
// So the universe was rediscovered from main run 33131296988 (b6003a45e), the first completed
// floor measurement after gunbc#9477. A future rebuild must use a post-#9477 measurement for the
// same reason; a charged-basis figure is not this roster's subject and never was.
//
// AND THEN FOURTEEN MORE WERE ADDED, from the first run that executed this mechanism at all
// (33136345225). That is the initial census completing rather than the roster growing, and the
// distinction is worth stating because this contract is shrink-only and an unexplained addition
// would look like a violation of it. Those fourteen are rows the 500ms ceiling caught that main's
// own 5000ms run could not have reported: seven were INTERRUPTED at 501-508ms CPU, having never
// reached a verdict, and seven completed over. A row cannot be discovered as over-ceiling by a
// measurement taken under a ceiling ten times looser, so the population was only fully knowable
// once the ceiling it is defined against was the one actually running. From here the direction is
// shrink-only in earnest.
//
// SIXTEEN FURTHER ROWS FAILED THAT RUN AND ARE DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. They exceeded on WALL while
// their CPU sat inside the ceiling, because fill is netted out of CPU and not out of wall, so a
// first-touch payer reads ~0ms CPU and a full shared-build wall. Rostering them would have frozen
// working witnesses for a defect in the wall clock's derivation -- the same error as the
// charged-basis roster, one clock over. They were fixed by re-deriving
// `required_floor_claim_wall_safety_limit_ms` against the population it actually has to clear;
// that constant carries the receipt.
//
// THE OPERATOR RULING THIS SERVES (2026-08-27). The per-claim ceiling is 500ms. It was set to
// 500 at gunbc#8283 (2026-08-17) and was raised twice without a ruling on the value: to 1552 at
// gunbc#8514, justified only by "measured-max plus one scheduler-quantum" over the then-current
// tree -- the tree-copied oracle DESIGN section 5 forbids -- and to 5000 at gunbc#8533, which
// cited an operator ruling that was about SPLITTING the CPU and wall clocks, not about the
// magnitude. The operator's quoted words in that diff, "DO NOT set CPU and wall to the same
// 5000ms", presuppose 5000 was already on the table; the value rode in as a passenger on a
// ruling about something else. That is the AUTHORITY SUBSTITUTION failure mode DESIGN names.
// The ruling of 2026-08-17 was never repealed. This roster restores it.
//
// WHAT MEMBERSHIP MEANS, STATED SO IT IS NEVER READ AS COVERAGE. A rostered identity is
// WITHHELD FROM EXECUTION. It does not run on the floor, it does not run in a long home, it
// does not run on a cadence. Its coverage is GONE while it sits here. That is a declared
// DESIGN section 4b(3) rung drop -- below -- and not a deferral: the operator's ruling is that
// these rows are broken, and a broken row does not get an exemption that lets it keep spending
// the budget it broke.
//
// WHY IN PLACE RATHER THAN MOVED TO test/claim/long/. Relocation is the move the 2026-08-04
// admission ruling forbids and that `gunbc.witness_deferral_freeze` exists to close: it deletes
// coverage while retaining the source, with nothing counting what was lost (the gunbc#7762
// specimen). The distinction is not the coverage outcome -- both stop executing -- it is that
// this roster is DECLARED, COUNTED EVERY RUN, IDENTITY-GRAIN, AND SHRINK-ONLY, and a relocation
// is none of those. The files do not move.
//
// THE MONOTONE DEBT CONTRACT (DESIGN section 5's fourth sanctioned oracle form), and each
// condition is load-bearing:
//   - the subject universe is INDEPENDENTLY DISCOVERED -- the floor measures every claim's
//     marginal cost itself; this roster is checked against that discovery, never authored beside
//     it;
//   - membership is at IDENTITY GRAIN, never a count. No witness asserts this roster's size
//     against a literal, because a number copied from the current tree is a snapshot;
//   - the direction is justified: a row leaves by being made cheap, and the forward hole is
//     already shut -- a NEW or REGRESSED row over 500ms simply refuses, because 500 is the
//     ceiling and nothing here admits an identity the floor did not already discover;
//   - a rostered identity the tree no longer carries REFUSES as a stale row, so the roster
//     cannot rot into a permission slip for witnesses that no longer exist.
//
// A KNOWN, BOUNDED IMPURITY IN THIS UNIVERSE, DECLARED RATHER THAN DISCOVERED LATER.
//
// The marginal basis above corrects attribution for ONE shared artifact and not for shared
// builds in general. `v1_compiler.cli_run` `record_shared_artifact_fill_cpu` has exactly one
// call site -- inside `compile_dag_rust_emit_check` -- so a claim whose cost is dominated by a
// DIFFERENT unbracketed shared build is still charged for work it does not own, and the
// subtraction reports zero for it. The known instance: gunbc#9428 memoized the sibling
// `compile_dag_diagnostic_census` without a bracket, so a census miss accumulates nothing.
// (Found by snappy-dove-250 and sleek-cat-45; the single call site and the census's missing
// bracket are verified here by code read, and the discriminating evidence is theirs -- main run
// 33131296988 carries 259 per-claim `[floor-shared-fill]` lines and none names a
// callable_candidate_ambiguity row, beside a 5812ms charge that is almost entirely fill.)
//
// SIXTEEN OF THE ROWS BELOW SIT IN A CENSUS-CALLING MODULE, and they are named so that this is
// a retryable list rather than an invisible one:
//   test.claim.arity_zero_import_refusal_witness.the_same_import_carrying_one_member_is_accepted
//   test.claim.callable_candidate_ambiguity_witness.a_bare_call_whose_only_declarer_is_reached_transitively_refuses
//   test.claim.callable_candidate_ambiguity_witness.a_listed_import_does_not_exclude_a_transitively_reached_homonym
//   test.claim.callable_candidate_ambiguity_witness.neither_green_source_refuses_and_neither_mis_resolves
//   test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_direct_call_witness.w_kernel_numeric_at_the_natively_realized_nat_is_admitted
//   test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_direct_call_witness.w_kernel_numeric_at_the_peano_nat_is_refused
//   test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_list_element_witness.w_declared_coproduct_member_is_accepted
//   test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_list_element_witness.w_optional_carrier_is_undecidable_not_refused
//   test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_list_element_witness.w_reachability_control_discriminates_on_the_name
//   test.claim.generic_lambda_parameter_binding_witness.a_lambda_argument_binds_a_type_variable_a_later_argument_determines
//   test.claim.generic_lambda_parameter_binding_witness.a_lambda_field_of_a_generic_record_binds_the_type_its_sibling_field_determines
//   test.claim.generic_lambda_parameter_binding_witness.a_lambda_parameter_bound_to_a_type_variable_can_reach_its_fields
//   test.claim.import_admission_closure_membership_witness_test.listed_name_resolves
//   test.claim.import_admission_closure_membership_witness_test.pool_coincidence_name_still_resolves_today
//   test.claim.import_admission_closure_membership_witness_test.selective_unlisted_name_still_resolves_today
//   test.claim.operation_admit_callers_inert_witness.operation_form_admission_refuses_unadmitted_caller
//
// HOW TO READ SIXTEEN. It is an UPPER bound on census-caused miswarding and not a count of
// wrong rows: only the claim arriving FIRST at a given source absorbs the fill, so some of
// these are legitimately over the ceiling on their own marginal cost. It is also NOT a bound on
// the general class -- any row dominated by another unbracketed shared build is miswarded and
// invisible here.
//
// `both_closure_edge_index` IS NOT SUCH A BUILD, and this clause previously called it the
// obvious next candidate and left it unverified. Settled, and confirmed here by code read rather
// than relayed: `v1_compiler.cli_run` `run_required_floor` calls `warm_bare_reference_edge_index`
// TWICE during strict-preparation -- once over the source roots and once over
// `witness_layer_roots()` -- and reports the cost as `[floor-phase] phase=shared-index-warm`. So
// both index identities the fold can reach are built and billed BEFORE any claim window opens,
// which is why that artifact needs no bracket and why the ~28s it costs reaches no row on this
// roster. (Runtime confirmation on run 33135617689 is sleek-cat-45's; the warm sites are this
// carrier's own reading.) Naming it as a suspect here would have sent the next reader to measure
// a thing that is already correct.
//
// THE WELL-POSED SUCCESSOR IS NOT A ROSTER QUESTION, it is a construction one, and it is
// sleek-cat-45's framing: an artifact is either PREPARATION-FORCEABLE, in which case it is
// warmed and billed to preparation as the edge index is, or CLAIM-FORCED-ONLY, in which case its
// fill is netted out and the split reported as `compile_dag_rust_emit_check` does. The census
// memo was in NEITHER arm. That "neither" is a WRITABLE STATE is the actual defect -- gunbc#9560
// closes one instance of it and the next memoization reintroduces it.
//
// WHY THIS MATTERS MORE FOR THIS ROSTER THAN FOR AN ORDINARY MEASUREMENT: a row frozen for cost
// that belongs to a shared build cannot take the exit below, because the exit is "make it
// cheap" and the cost is not its own to reduce. It would sit here looking exactly like debt.
// TRIGGER: when gunbc#9560 lands the missing census bracket, RE-MEASURE THESE SIXTEEN and delete
// the lines that fall under the ceiling. That is a specific, dated, bounded action against a
// named list, which is the difference between a declared impurity and a silent one.

// HOW A ROW LEAVES, AND WHY THAT MAKES THE ROSTER SELF-CORRECTING. Delete its line. The floor
// then runs it under the 500ms ceiling and it either passes or fails on its own marginal cost.
// Nothing here needs to be re-measured to release a row, and nothing may be added to release
// one.

// THE ROSTER IS EMPTY, AND AN EMPTY ROSTER IS THE CORRECT LANDING STATE RATHER THAN AN UNFINISHED
// ONE. What stands below is the MECHANISM -- the membership test, the decline arm it feeds in
// `v2.workflow.required_floor`, the partition term, and the two-way staleness join -- with no
// identity enrolled in it. Nothing is withheld, so no coverage is deleted, so there is no §4b(3)
// rung drop to declare. The drop that stood here while this roster held 217 identities is deleted
// rather than annotated: a declared drop with an empty population is not a cautious drop, it is a
// false one, and it would keep a class reading as degraded while nothing was degraded.
//
// WHY IT IS EMPTY, AND THIS IS THE LOAD-BEARING PART. A roster keyed on a CHARGED figure is not
// monotone, and the failure is structural rather than a matter of measurement quality.
//
//   Fill is paid INSIDE execution, on a thread-local memo that starts empty. A withheld row does
//   not execute. So withholding a first-touch payer does not remove its fill -- it MOVES the fill
//   to whichever claim next names those sources, which then goes over the ceiling and becomes
//   eligible for this roster in turn.
//
// A contract that grows by the mechanism intended to drain it is not a debt contract. Worse, it
// would pass every witness written about it, because each individual row would be correct: the
// successor really did measure over, on the run where it was measured. The defect is invisible at
// row grain and only appears when the roster is read as a population over time.
//
// THE KEYING LAW, and it is what makes the contract monotone BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by
// hoping discovery order is stable (DESIGN §5, construction over validation): AN IDENTITY MAY BE
// ENROLLED HERE ONLY ON ITS MARGINAL CPU FIGURE, never on its charged total. Marginal cost is a
// property of the ROW -- it is what that claim's own evaluation cost once the shared artifact it
// merely touched first is attributed to the artifact -- so declining a marginal-over row moves
// nothing to anyone, and the population cannot regenerate itself.
//
// WHY THAT EMPTIES IT RATHER THAN SHRINKING IT. The 217 identities that stood here were
// discovered on a charged basis. Measured on run 33136345225, every row in this corpus whose fill
// alone exceeds 2000ms carries a marginal figure of 0-2ms, and the count of rows anywhere in that
// run with marginal CPU above 500ms is ZERO. The charged basis was not merely imprecise about
// which rows belonged; it was measuring a different quantity, one that is a fact about traversal
// order rather than about any row. So the honest marginal-basis population is not a subset of the
// charged one to be filtered down -- it has to be discovered fresh, and it may well be empty.
//
// That is the state this lands in: the ceiling restored to the operator's 500ms, the withholding
// mechanism present and executing, and nothing enrolled in it. If the fold then refuses on a row
// whose MARGINAL figure exceeds the ceiling, that row is a genuine over-cost witness -- provably
// not a payer for someone else's compile -- and it is enrolled here with its measured marginal
// figure and its run cited. Until such a row is measured, enrolling anything would be freezing
// coverage on a number that was never about the row.
// NO RUNG DROP IS DECLARED WHILE THIS ROSTER IS EMPTY, DELIBERATELY. §4b(3) requires a drop to
// carry a bounded population; an empty roster withholds nothing, so there is nothing lost to
// restore. A drop row kept "in case" would be inflation from the other direction -- a class
// reported as degraded that is not -- and it would rank for a restoration with nothing to
// restore. The drop returns with the population the moment any identity is enrolled.
fn floor_cost_debt_chunks() -> List<List<String>> {
  Empty {}
}

fn floor_cost_debt_roster() -> List<String> {
  list_flat_map(xs: floor_cost_debt_chunks(), f: fn(chunk) { chunk })
}

// THE MEMBERSHIP TEST. A `Bool` over a roster is the right shape here and not the mechanical
// one DESIGN warns about: the question this answers has exactly two states -- withheld or not --
// and the typed disposition that carries WHY lives in `v2.workflow.required_floor`, which is
// where a consumer that needs the reason reads it.
fn floor_cost_debt_holds(name: String) -> Bool {
  any(xs: floor_cost_debt_roster(), predicate: fn(row) { row == name })
}

